        <mxCell id="p2-40" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="ChapterBO: deleteChapter(id, confirmed) changes nothing and returns a failed result when confirmed is false (UC-01 alternative flow). When true it calls dalFacade.deleteChapterCascade(id), so components and glossary entries are removed in one transaction. getDeleteWarning(id) lists what will also be deleted (BR-05)." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="77" width="700" x="40" y="1540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2-49" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="ChapterStructureBO (proposed): configureStructure should merge with the existing components. Keep componentId and content for types that stay, create new components for added types, then pass the merged list to saveStructure. Otherwise reordering or adding a component would wipe content entered through UC-03." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="77" width="700" x="800" y="1540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2-58" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="ChapterContentBO: removeContent skips ContentValidator and calls updateComponentContent(id, empty string). It must NOT call deleteComponent, otherwise the chapter structure breaks. isChapterComplete treats a GLOSSARY component as complete when getEntriesByChapterId returns at least 1 entry; all other types need non-blank content. (Proposed: saveContent and removeContent reject GLOSSARY components; glossary data belongs to UC-04.)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="94" width="700" x="1560" y="1540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="p2-67" parent="1" style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;spacingLeft=6;fillColor=#fff2cc;strokeColor=#d6b656;" value="GlossaryBO: before calling dalFacade to add or update, isPersianWordTaken() runs. If the Persian word already exists in any chapter glossary (ignoring the entry being edited, excludeEntryId), the entry is rejected. The validator only checks emptiness and format. (Proposed: normalise the word, e.g. trim and unify Arabic and Persian letter forms, before comparing.)" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="94" width="700" x="2320" y="1540" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
